es 7 cards but is riskier. So the four_with_pair is better for both removing more cards and being a strong move. \n\nTherefore, the best move is to play the four_with_pair: ♠3 ♥3 ♣3 ♦3, ♥5 ♣5, and ♠6 ♥6. That uses up the 3s, 5s, and 6s, which are lower cards, and opens up the possibility to play higher cards later. This move is safe and removes a large number of cards, helping to deplete the hand quickly.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: Playing the four_with_pair move removes 8 cards (four 3s, two 5s, two 6s), which is the largest possible play available. This clears a significant portion of the hand immediately and uses the highest quad (3s) to establish dominance. The move is unassailable by peasants since no higher quad exists (only three 2s remain in play), and it preserves critical high cards (A, K, jokers) for later. \n\nReason: The four_with_pair maximizes card removal while leveraging the quad\'s strength to control the game. It eliminates lower-value cards (3s, 5s, 6s) that are harder to play later and avoids wasting bombs/rockets prematurely. This sets up a strong early lead, forcing peasants to either pass or risk overcommitting with weaker cards.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3", "♣3", "♦3", "♥5", "♣5", "♠6", "♥6"]}'}
